{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019ZCqT8Dmt2y8y7cuFyeD3m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both `go build` and `go vet` pass with no errors.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **`pkg/sys/signal.go`** (new) — Implements `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` with `sync.Once` to ensure idempotent handler installation. Uses a buffered channel (capacity 1) with `signal.Notify` for `SIGPIPE`, and a goroutine that calls `os.Exit(0)` on receipt, matching GNU coreutils behavior (srd002-sys R1.5, R1.6).\n\n2. **`pkg/sys/terminal.go`** (modified) — Implements `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` with SIGWINCH handling. Maintains a mutex-protected slice of callbacks in registration order. Uses `sync.Once` to start a single listener goroutine that loops on the signal channel, queries `TerminalWidth()`, and invokes all callbacks with the new width (srd002-sys R2.6, R3.1, R3.2).\n\n3. **`pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`** (removed) — The empty `InstallSIGPIPEHandler` stub was replaced by the real implementation in `signal.go`.\n\n**Acceptance criteria verified:**\n- **AC1**: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler` uses `sync.Once` — multiple calls are no-ops, no panic or duplicate handlers.\n- **AC2**: `OnTerminalResize` appends to the callback list and returns immediately — does not block.\n- **AC3**: The listener goroutine calls `TerminalWidth()` on SIGWINCH and passes the width to all callbacks.\n- **AC4**: `go build ./pkg/sys/...` and `go vet ./pkg/sys/...` both succeed with no errors."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116,"cache_read_input_tokens":82418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f925e3bd-1225-4c4f-a60e-443f7116398f","uuid":"c05a7415-e9c8-49cb-bbaa-9d23725b0395"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":114830,"duration_api_ms":114433,"num_turns":8,"result":"Both `go build` and `go vet` pass with no errors.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **`pkg/sys/signal.go`** (new) — Implements `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` with `sync.Once` to ensure idempotent handler installation. Uses a buffered channel (capacity 1) with `signal.Notify` for `SIGPIPE`, and a goroutine that calls `os.Exit(0)` on receipt, matching GNU coreutils behavior (srd002-sys R1.5, R1.6).\n\n2. **`pkg/sys/terminal.go`** (modified) — Implements `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` with SIGWINCH handling. Maintains a mutex-protected slice of callbacks in registration order. Uses `sync.Once` to start a single listener goroutine that loops on the signal channel, queries `TerminalWidth()`, and invokes all callbacks with the new width (srd002-sys R2.6, R3.1, R3.2).\n\n3. **`pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`** (removed) — The empty `InstallSIGPIPEHandler` stub was replaced by the real implementation in `signal.go`.\n\n**Acceptance criteria verified:**\n- **AC1**: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler` uses `sync.Once` — multiple calls are no-ops, no panic or duplicate handlers.\n- **AC2**: `OnTerminalResize` appends to the callback list and returns immediately — does not block.\n- **AC3**: The listener goroutine calls `TerminalWidth()` on SIGWINCH and passes the width to all callbacks.\n- **AC4**: `go build ./pkg/sys/...` and `go vet ./pkg/sys/...` both succeed with no errors.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f925e3bd-1225-4c4f-a60e-443f7116398f","total_cost_usd":0.8645782499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71223,"cache_read_input_tokens":564779,"output_tokens":5480,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71223,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens"